geometric-probability-af59501d.conceptual_definition:
The formula states that entropy (
S
) is proportional to the logarithm of the phase space volume (
$V_{phase}$
). This relationship is a cornerstone of statistical mechanics, linking the macroscopic thermodynamic property of entropy to the microscopic states of a system. It quantifies the number of possible microstates corresponding to a given macrostate, where a larger phase space volume implies a greater number of accessible microstates and thus higher entropy.
